Labnet fee oracle for Bitcoin Knots v29.2.knots20251110.

Adds -feeoraclefile=<file> and -feeoraclemaxage=<seconds> (default 600). While
the file's "t" is at most that old, fee estimates come from its "estimates"
(mainnet sat/vB by confirmation target, written by the Labnet's fee oracle):
for a requested target N, the smallest target in the file >= N (the largest
if N is above all), converted to sat/kvB and rounded, with that target as the
returned one, raised to the lowest fee rate this version's estimator can return
(MIN_BUCKET_FEERATE, 1000 sat/kvB): mainnet's Esplora runs a newer Core that
estimates below it, which this version never does. The estimate mode does not
change the answer. The RPC and the
wallet's internal call both go through the hook in CBlockPolicyEstimator::estimateSmartFee(),
so the wallet's own logic around the estimate is unchanged. When the option is
unset or the file is missing, stale, unreadable or has no estimates, the node
behaves as unpatched; each change of state is logged once.

The code is in a new file (fee_oracle.cpp), plus the options in init.cpp and a
functional test (test/functional/feature_fee_oracle.py).

